  "profiledPatchSha256": "86ae423ba938549cd9df43d3a79a9646fcde2d407f62e91cce4399126e5b2d88",
  "method": "Real public-mainnet archive reads with existing per-connection counters. Each scenario compares a warm idle minute with two triggers thirty seconds apart. Only counters are exported; no account identifiers, arguments, response values, credentials, or user data are included.",
  "cadence": {
    "measuredIntervalMs": 30000,
    "implementedIntervalMs": 300000,
    "activation": "An active MyVault subscription; startup, frame, and manual refreshes remain unchanged. Unsubscribe clears the timer and overlapping checks share one refresh promise.",
    "operatorHttp": "One capability GET per check, plus one pending GET per page of up to 100 requests. At five minutes, a single-page mailbox adds 0.4 operator-server HTTP requests per minute on every network.",
    "routing": "Pending mailbox pages query the operator local node for its finalized vault ID, with configured public archive fallback. Desktop skips verification for empty mailboxes and unchanged successfully verified requests. New, amended, or blocked items use existing verification; historical creation/removal snapshots may use public archive even with a healthy local node.",
    "fiveMinuteEstimate": "The final interval has ten times fewer triggers than the measured interval. Applying measured per-trigger costs gives about 0.8 public requests/minute for server archive fallback and 1 public request/minute per early-blocked item. These are estimates, not five-minute observations or upper bounds for deeper verification.",
    "sourceFanout": "Full verification of a current nonremoved lock performs 9 storage reads, a creation block-hash read, and snapshot setup before caching. Removed locks add the supplied removal block/hash/header, parent/removal event snapshots, historical locks/funding references, and parent release state. Bitcoin verification sends 5 Esplora HTTP requests plus 2 per retained funding input, using cache:no-store. Signing retains its existing fresh checks.",
    "limits": "Warm query/verification work only. Cold startup, auth, pagination, local-node probes, successful/deep removed-lock verification, Bitcoin provider traffic, and unrelated server workflows were not measured. These profiles establish selected request costs, not public-server capacity. Normal local-node lookup traffic is separate from public fallback."
